--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- two chain-polyester-chain legs, viscoelastic and Syrope polyester, on a floater in a JONSWAP sea, 60 s
-- Two parallel legs 50 m apart from one floater, each a 100 m studless chain at the fairlead,
-- a 400 m polyester section and a 250 m chain at the anchor in 200 m of water, with the anchor
-- radius of composite_chain_syrope_chain.dat. The polyester of line 1 follows the viscoelastic
-- (series-Kelvin) law, MoorDyn ElasticMod 2: EA = Es|Ed, the static and dynamic stiffness,
-- BA = Bs|Bd. That of line 2 follows the Syrope working-curve model with the
-- settings and OWC table of syrope_polyester_mooring.dat: the static start puts every polyester
-- element on its rest curve, and the dynamic stiffness alpha + beta * mean load governs the wave
-- response. The floater moves in a long-crested JONSWAP sea (Hs 6 m, Tp 11 s, gamma 3.3, along
-- +X, ramped in over 15 s) by the illustrative RAO table data/vessel/sample_rao.txt (vesselRAO),
-- which carries both fairleads, 14 m below the surface; the same waves load the lines. Both
-- legs see the same motion and wave kinematics, so their tensions compare the two rope models:
-- the static stiffness sets the different pretensions (Es against the OWC), the dynamic
-- stiffness the wave-frequency tension range.
--   chain 155 mm R4 studless: volume-equivalent diam 0.2791 m, dry mass 480.93 kg/m, EA 2.058e9 N.
--   polyester 181.8 mm: diam 0.1438 m, dry mass 22.42 kg/m.
